{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1786504370,"nonce":"ZPH+gLHT6Ge/zsRX7tq9Z3qTEX4=","title":"The closed EventType enum is re-declared as 18 raw string constants in four packages, and 21 of its 36 values have no Go caller","was":"**What is wrong.** `internal/alerts/domain/event.go` models `alert_events.type` as a closed value-object enum — 36 `EventType` values, an unexported `s string`, and `NewEventType` as the only parser. Four other packages then re-declare 18 of those same values as bare `string` constants and use the copies. The kernel type is never named outside its own module."}]}